{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-127266","model_call":16,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":8765,"output_tokens":282,"total_tokens":9047,"cached_tokens":7936,"reasoning_tokens":98},"output_characters":824,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1082813673#6_1510639763","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is focused on e-waste being shipped to developing countries and directly supports a key recycling challenge: exported/imported e-waste is processed in regions where lead, mercury, and other heavy metals contaminate soil and water, creating serious health and environmental risks.","learned":"A key challenge is preventing e-waste exports to developing countries where processing contaminates soil and water with heavy metals such as lead and mercury."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1632","reason":"This query found direct evidence on why e-waste recycling/disposal is difficult and hazardous, so continue for more documents that explicitly discuss difficulty, hazardous materials, and mixed material recovery."}}}
